<title>UK: Swedish debt office sees balanced budget in 1998.</title>
<headline>Swedish debt office sees balanced budget in 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish National Debt Office governor Thomas Franzen said on Tuesday a balanced budget was expected in 1998 and surpluses afterwards in Sweden.</p>
<p>&quot;For 1998, a balanced budget is expected and after that the government plans for budget surpluses,&quot; he said in a speech prepared for delivery at a seminar in London.</p>
<p>&quot;Consequently there should be gradual reduction in the absolute debt level,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
</text>
